In Angular, a binding expression is a segment of code within a template that Angular evaluates to dynamically synchronize data between your TypeScript component class and the HTML view. [1, 2]  
Types of Binding Expressions 
Angular categorizes bindings depending on how data flows: 

• Interpolation: Data flows from component to view using double curly braces . 
• Property Binding: Data flows from component to a element's property using square brackets . 
• Event Binding: Data flows from view to component to handle user interactions using parentheses . 
• Two-Way Binding: Continuous synchronization using the "banana-in-a-box" syntax . [1, 3, 6, 7, 8]  

